# The wheel scrolls the text by two lines and takes the cursor along when it would leave the
# window; over the title bar, the help lines and past the right edge it does nothing, over the
# status bar it scrolls too. Each turn wears the message on the status bar down by three keys, so
# it is gone after the seventh. One report to a step: a terminal sends them one by one, and
# several in one write are not handled alike by ncurses. Coordinates are counted from 1.
args: --mouse t.txt
size: 40x12
file t.txt:
| line 01 of the file
| line 02 of the file
| line 03 of the file
| line 04 of the file
| line 05 of the file
| line 06 of the file
| line 07 of the file
| line 08 of the file
| line 09 of the file
| line 10 of the file
| line 11 of the file
| line 12 of the file
| line 13 of the file
| line 14 of the file
| line 15 of the file
| line 16 of the file
| line 17 of the file
| line 18 of the file
| line 19 of the file
| line 20 of the file
| line 21 of the file
| line 22 of the file
| line 23 of the file
| line 24 of the file
| line 25 of the file
| line 26 of the file
| line 27 of the file
| line 28 of the file
| line 29 of the file
| line 30 of the file
| line 31 of the file
| line 32 of the file
| line 33 of the file
| line 34 of the file
| line 35 of the file
| line 36 of the file
| line 37 of the file
| line 38 of the file
| line 39 of the file
| line 40 of the file
keys: {Mouse 65 5 4 M}
